lid #ddd;'>Local brands, new D2C</td></tr><tr><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'><strong>10K-50K (Micro)</strong></td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>$200-$1,000</td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>$10-$25</td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>Most common brand tier</td></tr><tr><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'><strong>50K-100K (Mid-Tier)</strong></td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>$1,000-$3,000</td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>$15-$35</td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>Major brand campaigns</td></tr><tr><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'><strong>100K-500K (Macro)</strong></td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>$3,000-$10,000</td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>$25-$50</td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>Premium brand tier</td></tr><tr><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'><strong>500K+ (Mega)</strong></td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>$10,000+</td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>$40-$100+</td><td style='padding: 0.75rem; border: 1px solid #ddd;'>Celebrity-tier rates</td></tr></table><p><strong>Rate multipliers:</strong></p><ul style='list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.5rem;'><li><strong>+50-100%</strong> for exclusivity (can't work with competitors)</li><li><strong>+25-50%</strong> for whitelisting/Spark Ads rights</li><li><strong>+20-40%</strong> for usage rights beyond TikTok</li><li><strong>+30-50%</strong> for rush turnaround (under 48 hours)</li></ul><h2 id='how-to-get-paid' style='color: #333; font-size: 1.8rem;'>How to Get Paid TikTok Partnerships</h2><p>Getting paid (not just gifted) requires positioning yourself correctly. Here's how:</p><h3 style='color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;'>1. Build a Track Record First</h3><p>Most brands won't pay creators with no brand experience. Start with:</p><ul style='list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.5rem;'><li>PR gifting (free products) to build portfolio</li><li>Tag brands organically in content</li><li>Share performance metrics when brand content performs well</li><li>Graduate from gifted to paid after 2-3 successful gifted collabs</li></ul><h3 style='color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;'>2. Know Your Numbers</h3><p>Brands paying for content want data. Know:</p><ul style='list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.5rem;'><li><strong>Average views:</strong> Your typical video performance</li><li><strong>Engagement rate:</strong> (Likes + Comments + Shares) / Views</li><li><strong>Audience demographics:</strong> Age, gender, location from TikTok analytics</li><li><strong>Past brand performance:</strong> How previous sponsored content performed</li></ul><h3 style='color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;'>3. Make it Easy to Pay You</h3><p>Professional setup = more paid opportunities:</p><ul style='list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.5rem;'><li>Business email in bio (not personal Gmail)</li><li>Media kit with rates (PDF or link)</li><li>Professional invoicing (PayPal, Stripe, or invoicing tool)</li><li>Contract template ready for custom terms</li></ul><h3 style='color: #26A69A; font-size: 1.3rem;'>4. Use Platforms That Connect to Paying Brands</h3><p>Instead of cold pitching, get discovered by brands already budgeted to pay:</p><ul style='list-style: disc; padding-left: 1.5rem;'><li><strong>TikTok Creator Marketplace:</strong> Official TikTok brand connection (requires 100K+)</li><li><strong>newcollab:</strong> Brands browse profiles and send paid offers (any follower count)</li><li><strong>AspireIQ, Grin, CreatorIQ:</strong> Enterprise brand platforms</li><li><strong>Hashtag Paid:</strong> Campaign-based paid opportunities</li></ul><a href='/register/creator?utm_source=blog&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=paid-tiktok-partnerships-brands-list-2026' style='display: inline-block; background: #26A69A; color: white; padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem; border-radius: 4px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; margin: 1rem 0;'>Get Found by Paying Brands</a><h2 id='faq' style='color: #333; font-size: 1.8rem;'>FAQ</h2><div class='faq-section' style='margin: 2rem 0;'><div class='faq-item' style='margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding: 1rem; background: #f8f9fa; border-radius: 8px;'><h4 style='color: #26A69A; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;'>How many followers do I need for paid TikTok partnerships?</h4><p style='margin: 0;'>Most brands start paying at 10K-25K followers, but it depends on your niche and engagement rate. Finance, tech, and app brands often pay nano-creators (5K+) because they care about conversions, not reach. Beauty and fashion brands typically require 15K+ minimum for paid campaigns.</p></div><div class='faq-item' style='margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding: 1rem; background: #f8f9fa; border-radius: 8px;'><h4 style='color: #26A69A; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;'>What's the difference between paid partnerships and PR packages?</h4><p style='margin: 0;'>PR packages = free products, no cash payment. Paid partnerships = cash payment (sometimes plus product). Both may require posting, but only paid partnerships give you actual money. Always clarify which you're being offered before agreeing.</p></div><div class='faq-item' style='margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding: 1rem; background: #f8f9fa; border-radius: 8px;'><h4 style='color: #26A69A; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;'>Do I need to disclose paid TikTok partnerships?</h4><p style='margin: 0;'>Yes, always. Use TikTok's built-in \"Paid partnership\" label in the posting flow. FTC requires clear disclosure of any material relationship with brands. Non-disclosure can result in FTC penalties and brand blacklisting.</p></div><div class='faq-item' style='margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding: 1rem; background: #f8f9fa; border-radius: 8px;'><h4 style='color: #26A69A; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;'>How do brands pay TikTok creators?</h4><p style='margin: 0;'>Common payment methods: PayPal (most common), bank transfer/ACH, check (rare), platform payout (if using creator marketplace). Most brands pay Net 30 (30 days after content approval). Some pay 50% upfront, 50% on delivery for larger campaigns.</p></div><div class='faq-item' style='margin-bottom: 1.5rem; padding: 1rem; background: #f8f9fa; border-radius: 8px;'><h4 style='color: #26A69A; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;'>Should I use a contract for paid TikTok partnerships?</h4><p style='margin: 0;'>Yes, always for paid work. The contract should include: deliverables (number of videos, format), timeline, payment amount and schedule, usage rights (can they use your content in ads?), exclusivity terms, and revision policy. Many brands provide their own contracts — read them carefully.</p></div></div><div class='cta-section' style='background: #f8f9fa; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 8px; margin-top: 2rem; text-align: center;'><h3 style='margin-bottom: 1rem;'>Ready to Get Paid for TikTok Content?</h3><p style='margin-bottom: 1.5rem;'>Join creators earning $500-$10,000+ per sponsored TikTok video.</p><div style='display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;'><div style='text-align: center;'><div style='font-size: 2rem; font-weight: bold; color: #26A69A;'>70+</div><div>Paying Brands</div></div><div style='text-align: center;'><div style='font-size: 2rem; font-weight: bold; color: #26A69A;'>$100-$10K</div><div>Per Video</div></div><div style='text-align: center;'><div style='font-size: 2rem; font-weight: bold; color: #26A69A;'>Updated</div><div>Monthly</div></div></div><a href='/register/creator?utm_source=blog&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=paid-tiktok-partnerships-brands-list-2026' style='display: inline-block; background: #26A69A; color: white; padding: 1rem 2rem; border-radius: 4px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 1rem; font-size: 1.1rem;'>Create Your Free Profile</a><p style='margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.9rem; color: #6c757d;'>Stop accepting free products. Start getting paid.</p></div></div>",
